{"text": "PRIVILEGED & CONFIDENTIAL -- ATTORNEY WORK PRODUCT\nLiebowitz & Marsh LLP -- Family Law Group\nInitial client mtg, file FL-2026-0318\n2/10/26, 10:30 am, conf rm B.  Present: DKL, R. Tanaka (paralegal), client.\n\nCLIENT\nMarisol Castellanos-Reyes (goes by \"Mari\"), DOB 07/22/1984, SSN xxx-xx-4388.\nCell 210.555.0164 (OK to text; do NOT leave voicemail on the\nhouse line, (210) 555-0109).\nEmail: mari.castellanos84@mailbox.example -- new account, husband doesn't know about it.\nStaying w/ her sister Guadalupe at 4417 Mesquite Hollow Dr., Apt. 12C,\nSan Antonio, TX 78209.\n\nSPOUSE\nHéctor Reyes Jr. (\"Hector\" on the tax returns), born March 3, 1981. Owns 100% of\nReyes Concrete & Paving, Inc. Married June 14, 2008 in Laredo. Separated since 11/29/2025,\nwhen Mr. Reyes moved in with Grace Okonkwo-Bell, the company's office manager.\n\nCHILDREN\nSofía (DOB 2011-09-02, 8th grade at St. Brendan's Academy) and Mateo (born 1/15/2016).\nSofía was diagnosed with ADHD last spring and takes Adderall XR 10 mg on school days;\nshe sees Dr. Anand Krishnamurthy every other Thursday. Mateo has a peanut allergy\n(EpiPen at school).\n\nWHAT SHE TOLD US\n1. Custody. Wants primary; husband wants 50/50. He had a DWI arrest in 2023\n   (Bexar County cause no. CR-2023-118842, pled to obstruction of a highway,\n   12 mo. deferred). He says he goes to AA but Mari found receipts from\n   The Rusty Spur in the truck. Best-interest factors under Tex. Fam. Code § 153.002\n   look decent for her -- she has done all school/medical since birth.\n2. Immigration. Mari became a U.S. citizen in 2019. Hector has said he will \"call\n   ICE on her mother,\" who overstayed a visitor visa and lives with Guadalupe.\n   Told her we will document the threat; her mother needs separate counsel.\n3. Money. He controls everything. Grace has been signing company checks\n   since December. Both families are devout Catholic; her mother-in-law\n   (\"Doña Carmen\") is pressuring her not to file.\n\nASSETS / DEBTS (per client, unverified)\n- House, 218 Encino Ridge, Alamo Heights -- bought 2014 for $389,000; she thinks it's\n  worth \"around six fifty\". Mortgage w/ Lone Star Teachers Credit Union,\n  loan # 0048-771203-9, bal. approx $214k.\n- LSTCU joint checking 7730041928; her own savings (opened Jan. 5) acct\n  ending 6612, about $3,200.\n- Condo in Port Aransas titled in the company's name -- the \"Pelican unit\".\n- 2022 Ford F-250, VIN 1FT7W2BT5NEC41873, plate TX KPL-4471, company-owned but\n  his daily driver. Her 2019 Honda Odyssey is paid off.\n- Reyes Concrete -- 2024 gross approx $2.1 million; she kept the books until 2022\n  and says he runs personal expenses through the company AmEx ending 2239.\n- Her income: teacher's aide at Northside Elementary, $31,450/yr.\n\nOTHER SIDE\nHe has retained Bartholomew Quigley III of Quigley Family Law, P.C.\n(bquigley@quigleyfamilylaw.example, 210-555-0177 x204). Bart will push mediation early.\nLikely judge: Hon. Lucille P. Vandermeer, 288th District Court. Judge Vandermeer\nroutinely orders a custody evaluation when ADHD meds are in the picture.\n\nTO DO\n- Retainer $5,000 by cashier's check; fee agreement signed today.\n- File petition + TRO request by Feb. 20, 2026.\n- Get 2022-2024 joint returns (Form 1040) and company returns from the CPA.\n- Send Mari the financial checklist via portal:\n  https://portal.liebowitzmarsh.example/intake/FL-2026-0318\n- RT to run asset search on the Port Aransas condo.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "532 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Marisol Castellanos-Reyes", "Reyes", "Bartholomew Quigley III", "Lucille P. Vandermeer", "Mari"], "companies": ["Liebowitz & Marsh LLP", "Reyes Concrete & Paving, Inc.", "The Rusty Spur", "Lone Star Teachers Credit Union", "Reyes Concrete", "Quigley Family Law, P.C."]}, "topics": {"places": ["San Antonio", "Laredo", "Bexar County", "Alamo Heights", "Northside Elementary", "Port Aransas"], "health": ["ADHD", "Adderall XR", "peanut allergy", "EpiPen", "St. Brendan's Academy", "Dr. Anand Krishnamurthy", "ADHD meds"], "sensitive": ["SSN", "immigration", "visitor visa", "Catholic"], "names": ["Marisol", "Mari", "Héctor", "Sofía", "Mateo", "Grace", "Doña Carmen", "Anand", "Bart", "Lucille"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 7.5, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 51, "end": 72, "text": "Liebowitz & Marsh LLP", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Liebowitz & Marsh LLP"}, {"start": 118, "end": 130, "text": "FL-2026-0318", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "FL-2026-0318"}, {"start": 131, "end": 148, "text": "2/10/26, 10:30 am", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "2/10/26, 10:30 am"}, {"start": 171, "end": 174, "text": "DKL", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "DKL"}, {"start": 176, "end": 185, "text": "R. Tanaka", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "R. Tanaka"}, {"start": 215, "end": 240, "text": "Marisol Castellanos-Reyes", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Marisol Castellanos-Reyes"}, {"start": 251, "end": 255, "text": "Mari", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Send Mari"}, {"start": 263, "end": 273, "text": "07/22/1984", "kind": "dob", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "07/22/1984"}, {"start": 279, "end": 290, "text": "xxx-xx-4388", "kind": "ssn", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "xxx-xx-4388"}, {"start": 297, "end": 309, "text": "210.555.0164", "kind": "phone", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "210.555.0164"}, {"start": 365, "end